I've never played spork before, and I haven't read any of the spoilers
(I don't think they exist yet), so I decided to try a game or two.
This is a review of my second game, first ascension (also first Spork
ascension on NAO).   I started taking "Stream of thought" notes at the
rogue level, so the first part is from memory.  Warning: it's long and
a bit spoily.  Also beware that I've only played very few games, so
some of my observations might be off, or even totally wrong (e.g. my
notes on Elbereth) ---> statistics of small numbers.

At the plane of Fire, the game got stuck, and it took me a day or so
for me to contact Paxed to get him to renew it.  Thank you.  Also
thanks to the authors of Spork.  There's a lot of good stuff in here.


knnn

---

My first game, I want to get as far as possible -- One Lawful Valk
coming up.   Started normally, went toward sokoban, and found bones
file.  Tried dipping for Excalibur, but got a cursed (rusty) sword for
my efforts.  Apparently dipping only works for Knights (since the
"hand comes out" routine still exists).  No problem, at least my first
gift a guaranteed to be another great weapon...  Wrong!  My first gift
is a bloody orcish ringmail (+4 to be fair, but still). The second
gift is a "shield of venom", which sounds useful.  It's also +4, so
ditch the small shield. It's not that easy to find sacrifices in the
early levels, but I guess staying around an altar can net you a
complete set of armor.  The next weirdness comes from eating corpses.
Every time I eat any corpse that can give (even more than one)
intrinsic, I get the appropriate message -- for *all* of them.  And I
keep getting them again and again.  It looks like Spork has some sort
of "partial intrinsic" system where you get more defended as you eat
more corpses (or maybe it's only a temporary defense?  That would be
really nasty)  [Post-edit:  It's a partial defense - see below].
P.S.  a "shield of venom" gives 100% protection to poison - tested it
out.  At one point I stopped getting "you feel healthy" messages, so I
assume I reached 100% poison resistance.  Found a magic lamp and
wished for SDSM, but wands/naga breath/beams only get partially
deflected...  Great.  :-(  Not sure what to do if I come across a
black dragon.  Maybe Cancel it?  Something in the mines jumped into a
poly trap and promptly turned into a purple 'L'.  I ran.  Another
weird thing:  Minetown looked like it was overrun by goblins (funny
layout, Iron bars, 7 candles in each "store").  It was also a bones
file, so I couldn't quite say what the story there is.  Sokoban had
the amulet, but it wasn't on the "Elbereth" space.  Something had
moved it, and it wasn't an elf.  I tried 'E' myself.  My current guess
is that it only affects neutral monsters (because orc, elves, ogres,
frost giants didn't get affected while "animals", hill giants did),
but it could be something more complicated.  If it is alignment based,
then there *might* be words for the other alignments.  Soko had
"Elbereth", so I don't know where you'd find the other possibilities
in game  [Post-Edit:  Looks like it's monster-level-based, not
alignment.  I just got unlucky].  Maybe the oracle (if it even
exists).   Donating to priests seemed to work normally, so my ac was
around -15 very quickly, but I still kept on losing too many
hitpoints.  The lack of a decent weapon for a combat-wombat like a
Valk is problematic.  Ended up losing to lack of hitpoints somewhere
below the big room.

