For my second game I tried a Wizard.  Since there's a lot of new
equipment (gnomish shoes, suit, helmet - all 0 ac base, shields of
poison protection, fire protection, wand of "wind"), I figured wizards
might show me what's what more quickly (+oID).

Started with a ring of slow digestion, so I immediately decided to
play *much* slower.  Up and down though the levels, found elven dagger
to use instead of staff.  Found early altar (dungeon level 3).  Sacced
a bit, and got orcish dagger +4 (not bad for any beginning character,
but I wanted magicbane).  Used scroll of identify (still costs 26), on
some rings and found one was +5 to damage.  Started wearing it
permanently.  Also started building up stash of throwing daggers. I
_think_ the +5 to damage works on thrown daggers but I couldn't say
for sure.  interestingly enough, Sokoban top level was "Bag of
holding" type, yet had an amulet of reflection.  Another interesting
note:  My Wizard did *not* start with a cloak of magic resistance.
She started with a cloak of protection (used my starting scroll of
Enchant Armor on it immediately).  Now normally, wizards can gain MR
pretty easily (quest, Magicbane), and protection gives you a little
better starting AC, but still.  It's interesting, I was running around
the same levels as before (with the valk), and with worse AC, but
things did not seem to be hitting as hard.  Maybe 'cause I was using
dagger-storm more often.  ("When in doubt, throw daggers"). Found
spellbook of Identify, and _that_ was a game changer.  Id'd everything
(slowly.  I have slow digestion).  Found I had an "amulet of Power".
This makes you regenerate PW faster (not much).  Alternated between
reflection and power for a long time.  Also found a cursed magic lamp
in minetown (only one shop - Itzchak's), and debated for a while what
I should be doing.  Ultimately ended up wishing for the Eyes of the
Overworld.  For the following reasons:

1.  Magic Resistance.
2.  To figure out the whole "partial resistance" thing.
3.  Replacement permanent light source for the lamp - good for dagger
throwing.


Also, I had found earlier that even *leather armor* does nasty things
to your spellcasting abilities, so the usual DSM wish sounded like a
problem.  Since I *do* want DSM later on, a robe would be useful,
which means getting MR through non-cloak methods.

Invoked the Eyes and sure enough found that I had MR, 5% sleep
resistance, 85% poison resistance, 15% fire resistance.  Got down to
the end of the mines.  Found a luckstone.  Various pets along the
(helped by spellbook of stone to flesh).

Got spellbook of "restore ability".  Unicorn horn doesn't restore lost
ability anymore, so this was helpful.  It always gives you the "you
feel good" message though, so you need to keep an eye on your stats to
know when you've cast it enough.

Found "iron safes".  Cannot open them with lockpick.  Not sure what
would work. [Post-edit:  stethoscope]

Made various stashes along the way.  Hit the quest and got thrown out
(not high enough level).  Killed a leocratta with thrown daggers.
Kept going down.  Fought a big-ass battle in the Big Room (second time
in a row.  Is it more likely to appear now?).  Became permanently
invisible by accidentally stepping on a magic trap.  At the time I
thought it was inconvenient, but it is actually useful for throwing
daggers, because you get a slightly better chance of picking them back
up when the monsters veer away in the wrong direction.  The downside
is that it's harder to lure monsters to an altar.


