donation for naked ac 1, but I only have about half the amount.

I get back down to Asmo, but forgot the black DSM.  Next time.  Sigh.
Interestingly enough, baby black dragons don't confer disintegration
resistance?  I continue going down.  Next level is the first wizard
tower level.  I carve some paths for the way back up, but my heart
isn't in it.  Something drops Firebrand.  Since I can't get skilled in
this class (yet.  I'm still hoping for an artifact) I put it away.
Next level.  I Find another Nazgul.  Decide to take him out now, while
the pickings are easy (dunno if I'll have the YDSM on the way back
up).

Next level.  Orcus.  I ready a scroll of scare monster a try out my
ring of conflict...  Conflict doesn't seem to do anything, just makes
me hungry (maybe the saving throws are much easier to hit now?).
Meanwhile, something reads a cursed scroll of create monster.  Then
something summons Yeenoghu.  Whole new ballgame!  I run to the
upstairs, chase him up, then wait for him so I can bring him back
down.  Pelt him with daggers and he falls.  Interestingly, I'm missing
some daggers.  Not sure where they disappeared.  One of the demons
drops speed boots.  Another snark is revealed to be a boojum.  I feel
more firm.  Finally find those daggers under a ton of rocks (giant
picked up all the boulders on the level).  I dig through to Orcus, and
fire away.  He runs and I wait for him on the downstairs.  We both go
down, but neither of us is on the upstairs.  I throw things at him,
and he falls.  Looking for my daggers again.  Sigh.  Find another
boojum.  A hit from it teleports me away (Like Quantum Mechanics).
Twice.  And there's a Nazgul on the level.  I get them both, but still
can't find my daggers.  Darn!  Onward.  Weird: Storm Giant just threw
a boulder _through_ a wall on DL 43!

In the wizard's zoo I mess up, and hit a disenchanter with my dagger.
It's now +6.  I Clean up the rest of the wizard's tower and head
back.  Oh yes,  Boots of Molasses slow you down.

Found that everything is still prettymuch 0% failure with a small
shield and no body armor.  I switch the Elven shield for a small one.
Need to enchant it up.  Head down to Minetown for candles.  Forgot
money. Sigh.  I finally pick it up (and a mummy wrap to get seen), and
I get the candles.  I also go to the quest to polymorph a better pet,
but the Poly trap dissappeers after a few uses.  Sigh.  :-
(  ....WaitaMinute!  I have a spellbook of create familiar!  ....Not.
Still trying to get better pets, I decide to write a spellbook of
charm monster.  Turns out it's *sixth* level spell.  I just wasted 40
charges of a Magic marker for nothing, but a recharge get's it to work
(Lucky, in retrospect).

I go back down to Vlad, and immediately charm a pair of white and red
dragons.  Going up to "Blackie" (I have the black DSM this time), I
meet yet another Nazgul.  Put on the Yellow DSM and kick his butt.
Meet a disenchanter on the way, but I'm carrying +0 Keowala exactly
for this!  Meet the Black dragon and melee him "You feel Firm".  I
believe that's 100%, but I'll check...  ...Yup.  Interesting: Black
DSM blinds anyone who hits you (passive attack, like acid blobs).  The
Eyes of the Overworld didn't show that.

- Another Nazgul in Orcus town.
- P.S.  You crack a safe with a stethoscope.  Finally find a ring of
levitation on the bottom floor of hell.
- Red dragon named Rhindle?
- Also, Blue DSM works like speed boots.

Drank all my potions of GL.  Sacced one more time and got Magicbane.
Getting artifacts is level related or was I just finally lucky?
Practiced with sleep until I could charm at 0%.  Got an extra wish
through potions, so I wished for SDSM.  Not quite using it right now
(yellow is better, and wearing DSM is too constricting for spell
casting).  Did alchemy.  Amount of max HP you get from potions goes
down as you quaff more.  Started getting max 4hp per potion, then
2hp.  Left 6 potions of FH for the end + whatever else I'll find.  In
retrospect, probably could have done better saving the potions for
later.  Next time.

Went down to the bottom.  Killed Rodney (cockatrice).  Did the
invocation.  Went into the sanctum.  Demogorgon Appears (middle of
graveyard)!!  Grrr...  Immediately pulled out holy water and dropped
scare monster.  Cured myself and started hitting him, but he ran (to
the inner sanctum I presume).  I try whacking him, but he doesn't stay
long enough.  I take my SDSM off to be able to cast cure illness at
0%.  Wait till he's away, then drank cursed potion of gain level to
get out and come back to the stairs.  I pick off another cockatrice
for the insta-kill (I deliberately leave 'c' alive for the ascention
run) , and then another Nazgul shows up.  I ignore him and head down
into a hellish group of monsters.  ...Finally manage to stand on the
upstairs and drop another scare monster (You can *throw* a scroll of
scare monster).  I miss Demo a bunch of times with the rubber chicken,
but finally succeed.  Whew!  Thank goodness even Demo respects scare
monster.  He drops the amulet...  At least I didn't have to fight the
high priest.

Things are going fine.  I'm running up the stairs, no problem.  No
mysterious force, so thing are fast.  I only wait around for
cockatrice corpses.  Then, at Medusa, trouble strikes.  A Titan
summons stuff, and the level begins to fill up (gremlins).  A magic
eye starts confusing me, A Lich start whacking on me, and the upstairs
are covered in monsters...

I'm in a bit of a panic, but I very carefully try to reach the
upstairs, and finally make it.  (Note to self:  Engraving on the
stairs on the way down is useful even in spork).

Something weird is happening.  It looks like there's monsters waiting
for me at every upstairs.  [Post-edit:  It looks like on the way up,
the upstairs spawns a new monster every few turns, forcing you to move
fast] I keep running.  Teleport scrolls don't seem to work at all (I
tried 10 in a row).  On dungeon level 18, I got the wizard.  Tried
hitting him with everything I had, but things kept missing.  Finally
nailed him and his clone with 3 zaps of a wand of death.

I keep running up.  Get to my stash, and pull everything in.  The
stash is right next to the upstairs, so monsters keep piling in.  :-)
I stock up, then continue running.  I make it all the way to the top
with no problem.  I have a cockatrice corpse handy for Rodney when he
shows up.  Earth is no problem.  I find the portal and head off.

Air is nasty.  With conflict a lousy proposition, and the fact that I
can't throw more than one dagger at a time means the easiest way to
get rid of those air elementals is either the finger or charm monster
(saving teleports for Astral).  I rely on the latter..0.  Even ac -33
isn't enough, and I hide in various vortexes and actually try to put
on the amulet of aethiopica while inside to gain a bit more power
back.  Ultimately, it's a run to the portal (the clouds go much
farther), and I make it just as a Ki-rin gets up to me.  I run through
without making sure all my pets get though.

Fire seems like the usual hassle.  I get pulled into a vortex as I
start, so I rest up a bit.  I get expelled, and the portal is about
half way across.  I start walking towards it, and a magic eye starts
giving me issues.  I Put my Yellow DSM back on while inside a fire
vortex.

Water is quiet.  I immediately detect the portal, put on YDSM, put on
a oilskin cloak and run for the portal.  Nothing attacked me.  I jump
to astral with an angel.

Astral:
Pest on the left.  Famine in the middle, Death on the right.  I enter
hungry.  Kill a vampire and dragon that are pestering me.  Lighten my
load and get ready.  Put on Robe.  Drop oilskin.  Get scare monster
ready.  Put on Free action.  Eat black dragon until I'm satiated.

Find a magic eye around the corner.  Kill it with daggers.  Ken the
Arbelaster wields Sting against me.  Priest of moloch in front.  Ken
is too well protected to hit easily.  I avoid him instead, but kill
all the priests at the choke points.  It takes me two potions of full
healing to get through to the first altar and back.  Famine is not the
problem, simply the amount of wailing I'm getting from the priests,
Angels, and summoned creatures.  I make a run for it, past Ken the
Arbalaster, and it's lawful (Ptah).  Out again.  Now, Pestilance or
Death?  I go for Pest (left), simply because I have cure sickness as a
spell, and he's susceptible to wands of death. I engrave Elbereth on
the ground in various places when I have the time.  Not for the
priests or angels, but simply to get the ants and bugs to block the
way for the heavier hitters.  ...Then Death comes for me from the
behind.  I kill him with a salvo of daggers and head right instead.
I've passed him already...

P.S.  Even if a lockpick is better for exercising dexterity, use a key
for the astral plane.  It's faster.  :-)  I see the high priestess of
anhur through the door (message that wand of lightning missed her), so
I'm pretty sure the right is chaotic, but I trudge on.  I get into the
inner room.  and sure enough, it's chaotic.  One altar left.  I run
around the high priestess of anhur (losing *lots* of hitpoints on the
way.  Another potion of FH coming up!).  Also losing some of my
daggers.  People are picking them up, so I can't always find them.  I
think that in general a bow + arrows would probably be better.  (Also,
enchanted launcher+ enchanted weapons =3D easier to hit monsters).  I
decided to simply teleport any player character monsters away (ac
-31).  On the way to the last room, I've got both pestilence and death
waiting for me in the corridor.  This means if I get them now, they're
all behind me (unless famine is somehow in front).  Daggers at death,
run past pest, getting Ill for my efforts, but a unihorn takes care.
I zap away another player character, and head into the last section.

Ran around some monsters.  Knock down pestilence *again*!  He doesn't
know when to give up.  Teleported things away.  Drank another potion
of full healing and ran to the altar.  Double checked everything, and
offered.


Total use of "unrenewable resources" on Astral:  6 charges of wand of
death, 1 scroll of charging (wand of death), 5 potions of FH,  ~10
charges of wand of telportation.


DONE!!

